SUMMARY:EPW 2026: Coffee session: Connecting long-term energy scenarios wit
 h marine spatial planning
LOCATION:Auditorium\, GIZ Campus Forum\, Friedrich-Ebert-Allee 32\, 53113 B
 onn\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:Marine spatial planning (MSP) determines how marine space is us
 ed and is a key enabler of accelerated\, responsible offshore wind deploym
 ent – a growing part of many long-term energy scenarios. This session ex
 amines how energy planners and marine spatial planners can work together s
 o that each process informs the other\, using more granular MSP data to im
 prove forecasts of timelines and infrastructure needs\, with a focus on in
 stitutional coordination and data governance.\n\nProvisional programme\, c
 heck for changes: https://energyplanningweek.info/#breakfast-msp
URL:https://energyplanningweek.info/#breakfast-msp
END:VEVENT
